From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:38:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] search_engines: drop remote new tab pages from prepopulated
 engines

TemplateURLDataFromPrepopulatedEngine() leaves new_tab_url empty. For a
non-Google default search engine, chrome/browser/search then uses the
local New Tab page instead of the engine's own, a remote site that
would be loaded on every new tab: DuckDuckGo, the default, defines one.

Why: search.cc prefers the engine's new_tab_url whenever it is set and
secure, with no switch or pref to keep the page local; clearing the URL
where engine data is built is the smallest change that has that effect.
Upstream: not upstreamable: product-specific behaviour

Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/components/search_engines/template_url_data_util.cc b/components/search_engines/template_url_data_util.cc
index 9e91d92e47ff9bc3c751802ac6f2073663e908ae..7e24fe031b3f6c864b52f0d53bd680e96c3ec098 100644
--- a/components/search_engines/template_url_data_util.cc
+++ b/components/search_engines/template_url_data_util.cc
@@ -346,7 +346,9 @@ std::unique_ptr<TemplateURLData> TemplateURLDataFromPrepopulatedEngine(
       ToU16StringView(engine.name), ToU16StringView(engine.keyword),
       ToStringView(engine.search_url), ToStringView(engine.suggest_url),
       ToStringView(engine.image_url), ToStringView(engine.image_translate_url),
-      ToStringView(engine.new_tab_url),
+      // No engine's own new tab page: it is a remote site, loaded on every new
+      // tab. Without one, chrome/browser/search uses the local page.
+      /*new_tab_url=*/std::string_view(),
       ToStringView(engine.contextual_search_url), ToStringView(engine.logo_url),
       ToStringView(engine.doodle_url),
       ToStringView(engine.search_url_post_params),
